    "ruleType": "detachment-rule",
    "group": "Blade of Ultramar",
    "summary": "Up to 3 times in the battle, as [your Command phase](vsdata:core-rule/command-phase) begins, you can pick a Combat Doctrine from the list below. You cannot pick one you already picked in the battle, unless a **MARNEUS CALGAR** model of yours is on the battlefield. The picked Doctrine applies to all your **ADEPTUS ASTARTES** units until your next Command phase.\n\n- **Devastator Doctrine**: the unit can shoot even if it made an [advance move](vsdata:core-rule/advance-move) that turn.\n- **Tactical Doctrine**: the unit can shoot, and can declare a charge, even if it made a [fall-back move](vsdata:core-rule/fall-back) that turn.\n- **Assault Doctrine**: the unit can declare a charge even if it made an [advance move](vsdata:core-rule/advance-move) that turn.",
